<title>UK: UK PSDR 4.393 bln stg in October.</title>
<headline>UK PSDR 4.393 bln stg in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK public sector borrowing requirement data for October. Deficits unless noted (rep).</p>
<p> PSBR (in bln stg)		  OCT     APR-OCT    APR-OCT</p>
<p>						    1996/97    1995/96</p>
<p> Public sector		     4.393rep  11.355    18.719</p>
<p> Central government		4.053rep  12.490    19.683</p>
<p> Central government own acct   4.452rep  12.664    19.232</p>
<p> Local Authority		     269	  308	 630</p>
<p>  from central govt		  410	1.190	 304</p>
<p> General Government		4.194rep  11.608    20.009</p>
<p> Public Corporation		  210rep   1.617rep 1.143rep</p>
<p>  from central govt		   11rep   1.364rep    147</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT RECEIPTS</p>
<p> Central govt total receipts   28.036   148.928    138.517</p>
<p> Inland Revenue receipts	 14.364    57.551     54.247</p>
<p>  of which income tax	     5.481    37.939     37.359</p>
<p>  corporation tax		   9.112    16.779     13.907</p>
<p> Customs and excise		 7.836    47.688     43.145</p>
<p>  of which VAT			5.468    28.721     24.789</p>
<p> Social security		    3.655    25.579     24.358</p>
<p> Interest				 550     4.445	4.469</p>
<p> Other				  1.631    13.485     12.298</p>
<p>CENTRAL GOVERNMENT OUTLAYS</p>
<p>  Total				23.585   161.593     157.750</p>
<p>   of which Interest		1.427    14.930	12.976</p>
<p>   Net departmental outlays    22.380   150.562     144.811</p>
<p>NOTE- Privatisation proceeds in October were 222 million stg, compared with 37 million in October last year.</p>
<p>Forecast was for a 1.5 bln stg Oct PSDR.</p>
<p>Corporation tax, totalling 9.112 billion stg in October, compared with a take of 7.320 billion stg last October.</p>
<p>September's PSBR was revised down slightly to 3.367 billion stg, the ONS said.  </p>
<p>VAT, income tax and social security receipts also rose, the ONS said.</p>
<p>The repayment is the largest October figure on record, the ONS said. PSBR records started in 1968.</p>
<p>November's PSBR will include a receipt of 900 million stg from the sale of Ministry of Defence married quarters. This will score as negative spending and will reduce net department outlays.</p>
